                  <provenance type="#e"><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_496">Sheen, Surrey.
                        Charterhouse of Jesus of Bethlehem</orgName><p>'Liber domus Jhesu de
                        bethleem de scheene ordinis carthusiensis quem scripsit domnus Johannes
                        Whetham monachus professus domus londoniensis eiusdem ordinis pro venerabili
                        patre d. Radulpho Tracy tunc priore dicte domus de Scheene, ad instancias
                        Reverendi patris &amp; domini J. yngylby tunc episcopi Landavensis, qui
                        etiam quondam fuit prior de scheene &amp; predecessor immediatus predicti
                        patris Radulphi Tracy a. d. 1496 Ad laudem dei. Amen.</p></provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Duke of Sussex (d. 1843). Sold 31 July 1844
                     as lot 203: see J. Pettigrew, Bibliotheca Sussexiana, lat. 49.</provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Ashburnham: see Historical MSS Commission
                     Report, 8, iii.104, no. 78: sold at Ashburnham sale, 1899, lot. 61. Bought by
                     H. W. Underdown.</provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Sotheby's, 20 June 1927, lot
                     459.</provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Tregaskis, Catalogue, 1000 (1931), no. 117,
                     with facsimile, and Catalogue, 1022.</provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Sotheby's, 26-29 April 1937, lot 252, sold to
                     Maggs for £21.</provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Rt. Hon. John Burns, sold on his death at
                     Sotheby's, 24 April 1944, lot 424. Subsequenlty owned b A. G. Hinds of
                     Richmond, and then by W. L. Wood of Chandlers Cross. It is in this location
                     that it is recorded in MLGB.</provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Sotheby's, 10 December 1969, lot 80
